.TH CURTSY 1 "August 2026" "curtsy 0.3.3" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
curtsy \- transparent TCP and UDP traffic forwarder
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B curtsy
.B --config
.I PATH
[
.B --check-config
]
[
.B --instance
.I NAME
]
.br
.B curtsy
.B --version
.br
.B curtsy
.B --help
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B curtsy
is a Linux TCP and UDP traffic forwarder. It listens on one configured address
and port and forwards traffic to one configured upstream without terminating
TLS or inspecting forwarded payloads.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR -c ", " --config " " \fIPATH\fR
Read the YAML configuration from
.IR PATH .
.TP
.B --check-config
Validate the configuration and resolved endpoints, then exit. Configuration
errors are reported on standard error and use exit status 2.
.TP
.B --instance
.I NAME
Optional instance identifier used only to prefix every log line with
.IR instance=\fINAME\fR
and to name the process; it never affects configuration, routing or
forwarding. The name must match
.B [A-Za-z0-9._-]
and be at most 64 bytes, a safe subset of systemd's template unit instance
names, so
.B curtsy@\fINAME\fR.service
passes
.IR %i
here.
.TP
.B --version
Print the program version and exit.
.TP
.BR -h ", " --help
Show usage information and exit.
.SH SIGNALS
.TP
.B SIGHUP
Reload the configuration. Invalid configuration or bind failures leave the
running configuration unchanged.
.TP
.B SIGINT, SIGTERM
Stop accepting new connections and exit gracefully. Existing TCP connections
are allowed to drain until the configured shutdown grace period expires.
.SH MULTIPLE INSTANCES
Several independent
.B curtsy
processes may run side by side, each with its own configuration, listen
addresses and hot reload. Give each an instance name so its log lines are
distinguishable:
.TP
.I systemd template
.B systemctl enable --now curtsy@\fINAME\fR
runs
.B curtsy --instance \fINAME\fR --config /etc/curtsy/instances/\fINAME\fR.yaml.
The
.B curtsy.service
unit remains the default single instance.
.TP
.I command line
Start a process per instance, each with its own
.B --config
path and
.B --instance
name.
.PP
Sockets for the same listen address and port carry SO_REUSEPORT, which only
groups sockets owned by the same effective UID. The
.B DynamicUser=true
template gives each instance a distinct uid, so instances cannot share one
listen address:port; set a fixed
.B User=
to share a port across instances. Shared ports are an intentional scale-out,
not automatic conflict detection. Each instance loads its own eBPF programs
(observer kprobes, sockmap, reuseport), so multiple instances coexist without
kernel conflicts.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/curtsy/config.yaml
Default configuration path used by the packaged
.B curtsy.service
unit.
.TP
.I /etc/curtsy/instances/\fINAME\fR.yaml
Per-instance configuration path used by the packaged
.B curtsy@.service
template.
.TP
.I /usr/lib/systemd/system/curtsy.service
Packaged systemd service unit.
.TP
.I /usr/lib/systemd/system/curtsy@.service
Packaged systemd template unit for multiple instances.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 2
Configuration loading, validation, or address resolution failed.
.TP
.B 64
Command line usage error.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR systemctl (1),
.BR journalctl (1)
